      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Source is a graphical chart (two stacked bars, 1918 and 1928, with percentages printed in the segments) plus two printed tonnage lists beside the bars; the printed figures are transcribed here as a table. Percentages are from the bar segments; tonnages from the side lists; totals from the side lists (also printed as 'Tons 80,247,706' / 'Tons 152,630,001' above the bars).",
        "American, German, Norwegian and Dutch are not shown separately for 1918 (blank cells = not printed).",
        "1918 side list prints the rows in the order British, Japanese, Other [Flags], Chinese*, with 'Other' and 'Flags' on separate lines interleaved with the Chinese line; read as Chinese* 21,782,704 and Other Flags 3,270,260.",
        "1928 Norwegian '3,786,532': the 7 is partly broken in the print but legible. Norwegian (3,786,532) is printed after German (3,703,228) even though it is larger.",
        "Total check (C03): 1918 Tons parts 80,247,706 = printed 80,247,706 — reconciles; 1918 percentages sum to 100.00 — reconciles.",
        "Total check (C03): 1928 Tons parts 142,630,001 vs printed 152,630,001 — does NOT reconcile (diff 10,000,000). Chinese* printed clearly '26,522,221' (= 17.38% of total) while the bar prints 23.93% (≈36.5 million); the discrepancy is in the source. 1928 percentages sum to 100.00 — reconciles.",
        "Check pass C03: re-read the 1928 side list (all eight rows + total), the 1918 side list and the Chinese*/American bar percentages from fresh crops; Norwegian '3,786,532' 7 is a diagonal stroke with a faint top bar — only a 7; no changes."
      ],
